claude-agent-acp exposes Claude Code over the Agent Client Protocol, the
editor/agent interface used by Zed, Marimo, Tidewave and JetBrains IDEs, so
any ACP client can drive Claude Code as its coding agent.

Upstream ships it as a Bun single-file executable, which has no FreeBSD
build. This port bundles the same JavaScript into a NodeJS single executable
application instead, and drives the claude binary from misc/claude-code.
